# =============================================================================
# TEST 112 — PERTURBATION ROTATION & SEMANTIC ENERGY DECOMPOSITION
# =============================================================================
#
# Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct · AkbasCore DRA
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PURPOSE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# TEST 111 established:
#
#   - physical perturbation ||δh||/||h|| survives deeply
#   - separator semantic displacement Δe strongly attenuates L11 -> L19
#
# TEST 112 asks:
#
#   WHERE DOES THE PERTURBATION GO?
#
# No controller.
# No gain tuning.
# No layer tuning.
# No new sensor search.
# No new prompt family.
# No random null.
#
# Same locked TEST110/111 system:
#
#   Model        : Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
#   Vectors      : exact ABOVE_IND / BELOW_IND recipe
#   Steering     : L10 + L11
#   IVME         : 0.10
#   sqrt(K)      : sqrt(20)
#   Prompts      : same TEST110/111 40 validation prompts
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORE DEFINITIONS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# For each layer:
#
#   δh_l = h_l^steered - h_l^baseline
#
# Layerwise semantic basis:
#
#   A_l = normalized ABOVE direction
#   B_l = normalized BELOW direction
#
#   S_l = normalize(A_l - B_l)      separator
#   C_l = normalize(A_l + B_l)      common
#
# Because S and C are orthogonal when A/B are unit vectors:
#
#   dot(S_l, C_l) ≈ 0
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENERGY DECOMPOSITION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Unit perturbation:
#
#   d_l = δh_l / ||δh_l||
#
# Separator energy fraction:
#
#   E_S = (d_l · S_l)^2
#
# Common energy fraction:
#
#   E_C = (d_l · C_l)^2
#
# Semantic-plane energy:
#
#   E_SC = E_S + E_C
#
# Orthogonal residual energy:
#
#   E_PERP = 1 - E_SC
#
# IMPORTANT:
#
# These are squared geometric projection fractions.
# They do NOT mean transformer "energy" in a physical thermodynamic sense.
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERTURBATION ORIENTATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   cos(δh_l, S_l)
#   cos(δh_l, C_l)
#   cos(δh_l, A_l)
#   cos(δh_l, B_l)
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAYER-TO-LAYER DIRECTIONAL CONTINUITY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   continuity_l = cos(δh_l, δh_(l+1))
#
# This measures whether the raw perturbation vector remains geometrically
# aligned between adjacent residual-stream outputs.
#
# It is descriptive. It is NOT by itself proof of causal "rotation".
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUMULATIVE ROTATION FROM L11
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   retention_l = cos(δh_11, δh_l)
#
# This directly asks how much the later perturbation direction resembles
# the perturbation present immediately after the final active steering layer.
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SEMANTIC PLANE ANGLE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Within span(S,C):
#
#   theta_l = atan2(proj_S, proj_C)
#
# This shows whether the perturbation rotates INSIDE the A/B semantic plane.
#
# If E_SC collapses while physical ||δh|| survives:
#
#   perturbation leaves the measured semantic plane.
#
# If E_SC survives but theta changes:
#
#   perturbation rotates within the semantic plane.
#
# If both happen:
#
#   both mechanisms contribute.
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT BOUNDARY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A/B vectors exist only L0-L19.
#
# Therefore semantic energy decomposition is L10-L19.
#
# Physical perturbation magnitude and raw directional continuity are measured
# through L27.
#
# No fake/interpolated semantic vectors are created for L20-L27.
#
# =============================================================================


